    "question": {
        "name": "CSEC Phy Jan 2023 Q5c — Electric Car Charging",
        "text": "<p>The battery in an electric car can be charged by passing a current of <strong>11 A</strong> through it for <strong>8 hours</strong>. The voltage used for charging is <strong>220 V</strong>.</p><p>Use the relationships: <em>Q = It</em> and <em>R = V/I</em> to answer the questions below.</p>",
        "general_feedback": "<p><strong>Model solution:</strong><br>Step 1: Q = I × t = 11 × (8 × 3600) = 11 × 28 800 = <strong>316 800 C</strong><br>Step 2: R = V/I = 220 ÷ 11 = <strong>20 Ω</strong></p><p>Common errors: forgetting to convert hours to seconds (×3600); using P = IV instead of R = V/I.</p>"
    },
